      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/26/493",
      "text": [
        " - «لاَ بَأْسَ بِأَنْ يُقَدَّمَ اَلرَّجُلُ وَ تُؤَخَّرَ اَلْمَرْأَةُ أَوْ تُقَدَّمَ اَلْمَرْأَةُ وَ يُؤَخَّرَ اَلرَّجُلُ. - يعني في الصلاة على الميت.\nوأفضل المواضع في الصلاة على الميت الصف الأخير، والعلة في ذلك أن النساء كن يختلطن بالرجال في الصلاة على الجنازة."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.493 - Hisham ibn Salim narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) that He said: \"There is no harm in placing the man in front and the woman behind or in placing the woman in front and the man behind\"\n[AL SADUQ]\nThis is referring to the arrangement of the funeral prayer for the deceased.\nThe preferred position in the funeral prayer is the last row, and the reason for this is that women used to mix with men during the funeral prayer."
        ]
      }
